broadband-modem-qmi: fall back to UIM card status on the last unlock attempt

Some Qualcomm firmware (UF896 v1.1 / MPSS.DPM.2.0.2) keeps returning
QMI_PROTOCOL_ERROR_UIM_UNINITIALIZED for the legacy DMS "UIM Get PIN
Status" command even when the card is fully ready and the UIM "Get Card
Status" path reports it present with PIN1 disabled.

The generic unlock-required check treated that error as retry-able, so it
retried the legacy command until the budget was exhausted and then failed
with "Couldn't get SIM lock status after 7 retries", leaving the modem in
"failed: sim-missing" despite a perfectly good SIM.

On the final attempt, fall through to the UIM card-status path instead of
giving up.  Retry behaviour is unchanged for firmware where the legacy
command works; only the terminal case changes.

--- a/src/mm-broadband-modem-qmi.c
+++ b/src/mm-broadband-modem-qmi.c
@@ -964,13 +964,28 @@
             return;
         }
 
-        /* Internal and uim-uninitialized errors are retry-able before being fatal */
+        /* Internal and uim-uninitialized errors are retry-able before being fatal.
+         * Some Qualcomm firmwares keep returning UIM_UNINITIALIZED for the legacy
+         * DMS command even when the card is fully ready and the UIM card-status
+         * path works; on the final attempt fall through to that path instead of
+         * giving up, so a working SIM isn't reported as sim-missing. */
         if (g_error_matches (error,
                              QMI_PROTOCOL_ERROR,
                              QMI_PROTOCOL_ERROR_INTERNAL) ||
             g_error_matches (error,
                              QMI_PROTOCOL_ERROR,
                              QMI_PROTOCOL_ERROR_UIM_UNINITIALIZED)) {
+            if (g_error_matches (error,
+                                 QMI_PROTOCOL_ERROR,
+                                 QMI_PROTOCOL_ERROR_UIM_UNINITIALIZED) &&
+                ctx->last_attempt) {
+                g_clear_error (&error);
+                qmi_message_dms_uim_get_pin_status_output_unref (output);
+                self->priv->dms_uim_deprecated = TRUE;
+                ctx->step++;
+                load_unlock_required_context_step (task);
+                return;
+            }
             g_task_return_new_error (task,
                                      MM_CORE_ERROR,
                                      MM_CORE_ERROR_RETRY,
